/.ref
/.vm
node_modules
web/.svelte-kit
# The frontend builds into the embedding Go package: //go:embed cannot name a
# path outside its own package directory, and refuses a symlink out of one.
# Contents are ignored but the directory itself is kept (a .gitkeep), because
# //go:embed all:build needs the directory to exist at compile time.
go/engine/http/spa/build/*
!go/engine/http/spa/build/.gitkeep
# Where it used to build, kept ignored so an old checkout does not commit one.
web/build
*.qcow2
*.log
.env
/.demo
# The development server's scratch tree: its data directory holding a master
# key and a TLS private key, its shares, the binary it builds and its log.
# scripts/dev.sh makes one at the repository root and `go run` makes another
# under go/, so the pattern is unanchored: an anchored rule covered only the
# first and let the second's private key be committed.
.dev/
# `go build ./cmd/<name>` or `./tools/<name>` from inside go/ drops the binary
# beside the source. One entry per command, because a bare `/go/*` would hide a
# new directory.
/go/differ
/go/enginedrive
/go/sc-engine
/go/sc-smb-agent
/go/stowcloud
# Runtime state the testbed compose stack creates beside its own file.
/deploy/testbed/data
/deploy/testbed/secrets
/deploy/testbed/smbcfg
/deploy/testbed/shares
# Unanchored: the token lands in `<data_dir>/setup-token`, and a data dir is
# wherever sc.toml points. The root-anchored form missed every dir but one.
setup-token

# Screenshots and fixtures left behind by browser verification runs.
# A broad `git add -A` swept four of these into a commit once.
.tmp-*
web/.tmp-*

# Gate tooling and cross-compiled test binaries: build products, not source.
/go/.tools/
/go/.testbin/

# CPython's bytecode cache, dropped beside a script the moment it is imported.
# The e2e helpers under scripts/ are importable, so this appears from a plain
# test run rather than from anything a developer did on purpose.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# SQLite files a hand-run server leaves wherever it was pointed. Three of these
# reached a commit from a manual boot inside the package directory; the tests
# themselves use temp dirs and never write here.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Internal documentation storage: proposals, feature requirements, security
# remediations, and engineering design notes. Only README-related documents
# are committed under docs/.
docs/internal/
